   'total_reps',
   'Finseth honors Adam Finseth, 40, a firefighter and EMT with the Burnsville Fire Department in Minnesota and one of the SWAT team''s two medics. A former U.S. Army staff sergeant who served two tours in Iraq, he died on Feb. 18, 2024, from a gunshot wound while giving aid to a wounded officer.

You have 18 minutes. Start with 83 wall balls (20 lb to 10 ft / 14 lb to 9 ft). With the time left, complete as many rounds as you can of 2 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), 18 push-ups and 24 double-unders. The wall balls can take a big share of the clock, and then the heavy cleans arrive with tired legs. Your score is every rep you finish before the clock stops.',
   '[{"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "83", "tip": "Full squat and hit the target on every rep. Break into planned sets, such as 5 sets of about 17.", "rx_men": "20 lb to 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb to 9 ft"}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "2", "tip": "Heavy for most people. Set your back flat and take each rep as a single.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "18", "tip": "Chest to the floor and lock out your arms at the top. Break early, such as 10 and 8."}, {"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "24", "tip": "Relaxed shoulders and quick wrists. Keep your jumps small."}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total reps, including the 83 wall balls.',
