   'Use a lighter ball or a lower target, and lower the power cleans to 135 lb / 95 lb or less. Push-ups can be done from your knees or with your hands on a box. Replace double-unders with 48 single-unders, or fewer double-unders. Cutting the wall balls to 50 gives you more time in the rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Finseth workout?", "answer": "On an 18-minute clock, 83 wall balls (20 lb to 10 ft / 14 lb to 9 ft), then as many rounds and reps as possible of 2 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), 18 push-ups and 24 double-unders."}, {"question": "How do you score Finseth?", "answer": "Count every rep you finish in 18 minutes, including the 83 wall balls. Each full round after the wall balls adds 44 reps."}, {"question": "Who was Finseth?", "answer": "Adam Finseth, 40, a firefighter, EMT and SWAT medic with the Burnsville Fire Department in Minnesota, and an Army veteran. He died on Feb. 18, 2024, while giving aid to a wounded officer."}, {"question": "Do the wall balls count toward my score?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit scores Finseth for reps on one 18-minute clock, so the 83 wall balls are part of your total."}]'::jsonb,
