   'Foo honors Sgt. Gary "Foo" Morales, 35, of the St. Lucie County Sheriff''s Office in Florida. The Air Force veteran had served the office for 12 years and had just been promoted to sergeant when he was shot and killed during a traffic stop on Feb. 28, 2013.

You start with 13 bench presses (170 lb / 110 lb) for time. Then you complete as many rounds as you can in 20 minutes of 7 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 77 double-unders, 2 squat clean thrusters and 28 sit-ups. CrossFit lists one barbell load, so the thrusters use the same weight as the bench. CrossFit does not say whether the 20 minutes starts before or after the bench presses, so choose one and note it with your score. The 77 double-unders are the longest station in every round.',
   '[{"name": "Bench Press", "reps": "13", "tip": "Use a spotter or safety arms. Touch your chest and lock out every rep.", "rx_men": "170 lb", "rx_women": "110 lb"}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "Your chest must touch the bar on every rep. Small sets keep you moving."}, {"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "77", "tip": "Break into steady sets before you start tripping. Relax your shoulders."}, {"name": "Squat Clean Thrusters", "reps": "2", "tip": "Clean into a full front squat, then stand and drive the bar straight overhead.", "rx_men": "170 lb", "rx_women": "110 lb"}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "28", "tip": "Touch the floor behind your head and your feet at the top. Use an abmat if you have one."}]'::jsonb,
