   'Fournier honors Mike Fournier, 52, a helicopter pilot who died on Aug. 19, 2020, when his Bell UH-1H crashed during a water-dropping mission on the Hills Fire near Coalinga, California. He was contracting with Cal Fire at the time. Fournier was a CrossFit Level 2 Trainer and began coaching at Cyn Gym CrossFit in 2011.

You complete 50 shoulder-to-overheads (115 lb / 75 lb), 40 burpees and 30 sumo deadlift high pulls (85 lb / 55 lb), with a 50 ft arm-over-arm sled pull after each one. You need a sled with a rope attached. CrossFit does not set a sled load, only that it should be challenging without needing long rests. The sled pulls hit your grip and back between the barbell sets.',
   '[{"name": "Shoulder-to-Overhead", "reps": "50", "tip": "Press, push press or jerk. Lock out overhead with the bar over your heels.", "rx_men": "115 lb", "rx_women": "75 lb"}, {"name": "Arm-Over-Arm Sled Pull", "reps": "50 ft", "tip": "Stand still and pull the rope hand over hand until the sled reaches you. Pick a load that keeps you moving."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "40", "tip": "Chest to the floor, then jump and clap overhead. Find a steady rhythm."}, {"name": "Arm-Over-Arm Sled Pull", "reps": "50 ft", "tip": "Sit your hips back and use your legs as well as your arms."}, {"name": "Sumo Deadlift High Pulls", "reps": "30", "tip": "Wide stance, drive with your legs, then pull the bar to your chin with high elbows.", "rx_men": "85 lb", "rx_women": "55 lb"}, {"name": "Arm-Over-Arm Sled Pull", "reps": "50 ft", "tip": "The last effort. Keep pulling without long breaks."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Choose a sled load you can pull without long rests", "Break the 50 shoulder-to-overheads early", "Steady burpees beat fast ones you cannot hold"]'::jsonb,
   '["Split the 50 shoulder-to-overheads into planned sets, such as 5 sets of 10, and use your legs to drive the bar.", "On the sled pull, keep your chest up and pull with long arm strokes so your grip lasts.", "Set the rope out straight before you start so the sled does not catch or turn.", "On the sumo deadlift high pulls, lead with your hips and let your arms finish the pull.", "Chalk your hands before each sled pull."]'::jsonb,
