   'Gage honors Nathan "Gage" Ingram, 27, of Trophy Club, Texas, a member of U.S. Navy SEAL Team 3. He was lost at sea on Jan. 12, 2024, while trying to save a fellow SEAL during a mission.

You start with a 1,996 m row. Then you complete 3 rounds of 12 power cleans, 11 back squats (155 lb / 105 lb), 3 rope climbs to 15 ft and 27 burpees. You finish with a 2,024 m row. That is just over 4,000 m of rowing, 36 cleans, 33 squats, 9 rope climbs and 81 burpees. The long rows bookend the work, so the last row starts when your legs are already tired.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "1,996 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you could keep for twice this distance."}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "12", "tip": "Quick singles or small sets. Keep the bar close.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "11", "tip": "Hips below the knees and a tight upper back. Use a rack if you have one.", "rx_men": "155 lb", "rx_women": "105 lb"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "3", "tip": "Use a foot lock so your legs do the work. Climb to 15 ft and come down under control.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "27", "tip": "Chest to the floor. Step back and step up if that keeps you moving."}, {"name": "Row", "reps": "2,024 m", "tip": "The last effort. Build the pace over the final 500 m."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
