   '["Row the first 1,996 m at a steady pace so you have legs left for the cleans and squats.", "CrossFit does not say how to get the bar onto your back. A squat rack next to your clean bar is the simplest setup.", "Set your feet flat on the rower and push with your legs before you pull with your arms.", "Pace the burpees so you can start the next round of cleans without a long rest.", "Treat the last row as a separate piece of work and break it into 500 m chunks in your head."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 115 lb / 75 lb or less. Replace each rope climb with 3 ring rows or a lying-to-standing rope pull. Cut the rows to 1,000 m each, or the burpees to 15 per round, if the full version would take more than about an hour.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Gage workout?", "answer": "For time: 1,996 m row, then 3 rounds of 12 power cleans, 11 back squats (155 lb / 105 lb), 3 rope climbs to 15 ft and 27 burpees, then a 2,024 m row."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Gage?", "answer": "36 power cleans, 33 back squats, 9 rope climbs and 81 burpees, plus 4,020 m of rowing."}, {"question": "Who was Gage?", "answer": "Nathan \"Gage\" Ingram, 27, of Trophy Club, Texas, a member of Navy SEAL Team 3. He was lost at sea on Jan. 12, 2024, while trying to save a fellow SEAL."}, {"question": "How do I get the bar onto my back for the squats?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Using a squat rack beside your clean bar is the safest setup."}]'::jsonb,
