   'time',
   'Gallant honors U.S. Navy Petty Officer 2nd Class Taylor Gallant, 22, of Winchester, Kentucky. He was assigned to Explosive Ordnance Disposal Mobile Unit 12 at Joint Expeditionary Base Little Creek in Virginia Beach, Virginia, and died on Jan. 26, 2012, during diving operations off the North Carolina coast.

You run a mile carrying a medicine ball (20 lb / 14 lb), then do 60 burpee pull-ups. Next comes an 800 m run with the ball and 30 burpee pull-ups, then a 400 m run with the ball and 15 burpee pull-ups. That is about 1.75 miles of running with the ball and 105 burpee pull-ups. Carrying the ball tires your arms and shoulders before you reach the bar.',
   '[{"name": "Medicine Ball Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Hold the ball at your chest or on your shoulder and switch when your arms tire.", "rx_men": "20 lb", "rx_women": "14 lb"}, {"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "60", "tip": "Do a burpee under the bar, jump up and do a pull-up with your chin over the bar."}, {"name": "Medicine Ball Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Settle into a pace you can hold. Shake out your grip as you go.", "rx_men": "20 lb", "rx_women": "14 lb"}, {"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "30", "tip": "Steady pace. Step back and step up on the burpee if it keeps you moving."}, {"name": "Medicine Ball Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "The last run. Push the pace.", "rx_men": "20 lb", "rx_women": "14 lb"}, {"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "15", "tip": "The finish. Keep the chin over the bar on every rep."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Switch how you hold the ball on the runs", "Start the 60 burpee pull-ups at a pace you can hold", "Small breaks on the bar save your grip"]'::jsonb,
   '["CrossFit does not say how to hold the ball. Switch between your chest, your shoulder and a bear hug to spread the load.", "Run the first mile slower than usual. The burpee pull-ups come straight after it.", "On the burpee pull-ups, jump into the pull-up so your legs help your arms.", "Set a rhythm on the 60, such as one rep every 10 to 15 seconds, and hold it.", "Put the ball in the same spot each time so you can pick it up fast."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter ball or run without one. Shorten the runs to 800 m, 400 m and 200 m. Replace burpee pull-ups with burpees and jumping pull-ups, or cut them to 30, 20 and 10.',
