   'rounds_reps',
   'Garbo honors Supervisory Special Agent Michael "Mike" Garbo, 51, of the DEA, who died on Oct. 4, 2021. Based in Tucson, Arizona, he spent his career fighting drug traffickers and worked across the U.S. and in Kabul, Afghanistan. He also practiced jiujitsu and other martial arts.

You have 21 minutes. Start with a 400 m run. With the time left, complete as many rounds as you can of 10 hand-release push-ups, 4 strict pull-ups, 20 kettlebell swings and 10 goblet squats (53 lb / 35 lb). Every round mixes pushing, pulling and hip work, so no single muscle group gets much rest. The strict pull-ups are short but get harder as your arms tire.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Run at a pace that lets you start the push-ups without a long rest."}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Lift your hands off the floor at the bottom of each rep, then press up as one unit."}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "4", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull your chin over the bar."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "20", "tip": "Drive with your hips and finish with the bell overhead.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Goblet Squats", "reps": "10", "tip": "Hold the bell at your chest, hips below the knees, elbows inside the knees.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Score is total rounds + reps after the 400 m run.',
   '["Do not sprint the run", "Keep the strict pull-ups as singles or doubles if needed", "One kettlebell does both the swings and the squats"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the pull-up bar, kettlebell and push-up spot close together so you lose no time between stations.", "On the hand-release push-ups, keep your body in one straight line from shoulders to heels.", "Break the 20 swings into two sets of 10 if your grip or back starts to fade.", "Keep your chest up on the goblet squats and push your knees out over your toes.", "Aim for steady rounds of about the same time from start to finish."]'::jsonb,
   'Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Replace strict pull-ups with banded pull-ups or ring rows. Lower the kettlebell to 35 lb / 26 lb, or swing to eye level instead of overhead.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Garbo workout?", "answer": "On a 21-minute clock, a 400 m run, then as many rounds and reps as possible of 10 hand-release push-ups, 4 strict pull-ups, 20 kettlebell swings and 10 kettlebell goblet squats (53 lb / 35 lb)."}, {"question": "How many reps are in one round of Garbo?", "answer": "44 reps: 10 push-ups, 4 strict pull-ups, 20 swings and 10 goblet squats."}, {"question": "Who was Garbo?", "answer": "Supervisory Special Agent Michael \"Mike\" Garbo, 51, of the DEA, based in Tucson, Arizona. He died on Oct. 4, 2021."}, {"question": "Does the run count in my score?", "answer": "The run comes first on the 21-minute clock. Your score is the rounds and reps you finish after it."}]'::jsonb,
