   'Garrett honors U.S. Marine Capt. Garrett T. "Tubes" Lawton, 31, of Charleston, West Virginia. He was killed by an improvised explosive device in Herat Province, Afghanistan, on Aug. 4, 2008.

You complete three rounds of 75 air squats, 25 ring handstand push-ups and 25 L pull-ups. That adds up to 225 squats, 75 ring handstand push-ups and 75 L pull-ups, with no equipment beyond rings and a bar. The ring handstand push-ups are one of the hardest gymnastics movements in CrossFit, and the L pull-ups add a core hold to every pull-up.',
   '[{"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "75", "tip": "Hips below the knees and stand all the way up. Steady sets of 25 work well."}, {"name": "Ring Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Kick up into a handstand on low rings, turn the rings out slightly and press to full lockout."}, {"name": "L Pull-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Hold your legs straight out in front, level with your hips, and pull your chin over the bar."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the 75 squats so your legs stay fresh", "Break the ring handstand push-ups into small sets from the start", "Keep your legs up on every L pull-up"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the rings low enough that your head clears the floor at the bottom of the handstand push-up and you can kick up safely.", "Squeeze your glutes and keep your body tight on the rings so they do not swing.", "On the L pull-ups, lock your knees and point your toes before you pull.", "Use small sets on the gymnastics from round one, such as sets of 3 to 5.", "The squats give your arms a break, so use them to recover."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace ring handstand push-ups with handstand push-ups against a wall, pike push-ups or dumbbell presses. Replace L pull-ups with pull-ups and tucked knees, regular pull-ups or ring rows. Cut the squats to 50 per round if needed.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Garrett workout?", "answer": "3 rounds for time of 75 air squats, 25 ring handstand push-ups and 25 L pull-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Garrett?", "answer": "225 air squats, 75 ring handstand push-ups and 75 L pull-ups, 375 reps in all."}, {"question": "Who was Garrett?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Capt. Garrett T. \"Tubes\" Lawton, 31, of Charleston, West Virginia. He was killed by an improvised explosive device in Herat Province, Afghanistan, on Aug. 4, 2008."}, {"question": "What is an L pull-up?", "answer": "A pull-up with your legs held straight out in front of you, level with your hips, for the whole rep."}]'::jsonb,
