   'time',
   'Goose honors Master Sgt. Chris Raguso, 39, of Commack, New York, of the 101st Rescue Squadron, 106th Rescue Wing, New York National Guard. A flight engineer and a member of the New York City Fire Department, he died on March 15, 2018, when an HH-60 Pave Hawk helicopter crashed during a mission in western Iraq.

This is a partner workout. The team completes 106 deadlifts (135 lb / 95 lb), then 7 rounds of 3 rope climbs to 15 ft, 15 thrusters with the same barbell and 15 kettlebell swings (70 lb / 53 lb). You finish with a 400 m run where both partners carry a plate (45 lb / 25 lb). CrossFit does not say how to split the reps, so share them in whatever way keeps you both moving.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "106", "tip": "Shared between partners. Flat back and the bar close to your legs.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "3", "tip": "Use a foot lock so your legs do the work. Climb to 15 ft and come down under control.", "rx_men": "15 ft", "rx_women": "15 ft"}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "15", "tip": "Full squat, then drive the bar overhead in one smooth motion.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "15", "tip": "Drive with your hips and finish with the bell overhead.", "rx_men": "70 lb", "rx_women": "53 lb"}, {"name": "Run with Plate", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Both partners run, each carrying a plate. Hold it at your chest or overhead and switch when your arms tire.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time.',
   '["Agree on how you will split the reps before you start", "Short, fast sets let both partners stay fresh", "Use a foot lock on every rope climb"]'::jsonb,
   '["A simple split is one partner working at a time and switching every few reps. CrossFit does not set a rule, so pick what suits your team.", "Swap often on the deadlifts and thrusters so neither partner''s grip or legs fail.", "On the thrusters, keep your elbows high in the front rack and drive through your heels.", "Keep the rope, barbell and kettlebell close together to cut transition time.", "Stay together on the final run, since you finish as a team."]'::jsonb,
