   '[{"question": "What is the Goose workout?", "answer": "For time with a partner: 106 deadlifts (135 lb / 95 lb), then 7 rounds of 3 rope climbs to 15 ft, 15 thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb) and 15 kettlebell swings (70 lb / 53 lb), then a 400 m run with both partners carrying a plate (45 lb / 25 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Goose?", "answer": "106 deadlifts, 21 rope climbs, 105 thrusters and 105 kettlebell swings for the team, plus the 400 m run."}, {"question": "Who was Goose?", "answer": "Master Sgt. Chris Raguso, 39, of Commack, New York, a New York National Guard flight engineer and New York City firefighter. He died on March 15, 2018, when his helicopter crashed during a mission in western Iraq."}, {"question": "How do partners split the work in Goose?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Split the reps any way you like, and both partners carry a plate on the final run."}]'::jsonb,
