   'time',
   'Gunny honors Command Sgt. Maj. Martin "Gunny" Barreras, 49, of Tucson, Arizona, senior enlisted adviser in the 2nd Battalion, 5th Infantry, 3rd Brigade Combat Team, 1st Armored Division. He died on May 13, 2014, of wounds from an attack on his unit on May 6, 2014. He joined the Marine Corps in 1983 and the Army Rangers in 1988, and Murph and Griff were among his favorite workouts.

You run a mile carrying 50 lb, then do 50 push-ups and 50 sit-ups. You repeat that, then finish with a third weighted mile. That is 3 miles of loaded running, 100 push-ups and 100 sit-ups. CrossFit lists 50 lb for the runs, in a vest, body armor or loaded pack, and does not say whether to keep it on for the push-ups and sit-ups.',
   '[{"name": "Weighted Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Wear a vest, body armor or loaded pack. Start at a steady pace.", "rx_men": "50 lb"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chest to the floor and full lockout. Break into sets of 10 or so from the start."}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Touch the floor behind your head and your feet at the top. Use an abmat if you have one."}, {"name": "Weighted Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "Hold the same pace as the first mile if you can.", "rx_men": "50 lb"}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Short sets with short rests. Your arms are tired from carrying the load."}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Steady reps. Breathe out on the way up."}, {"name": "Weighted Run", "reps": "1 mile", "tip": "The last mile. Push the pace.", "rx_men": "50 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Fit the load snug before the first run", "Break the push-ups early", "Pace the first mile, not the last"]'::jsonb,
   '["Strap the vest or pack tight and high so it does not bounce on the runs.", "Keep your push-up sets the same size each time, so the second 50 feels like the first.", "Split the 50 push-ups into planned sets, such as 5 sets of 10, before your arms fail.", "Decide before you start whether you will take the load off for the push-ups and sit-ups, and do the same each time you repeat the workout.", "Shorten your stride and keep your feet under you when the load starts to pull you forward."]'::jsonb,
   'Lighten the load to 20 lb or 30 lb, or run without one. Do push-ups from your knees or with your hands on a box. Shorten each run to 800 m, or cut the push-ups and sit-ups to 25 each.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Gunny workout?", "answer": "For time: 1 mile weighted run, 50 push-ups, 50 sit-ups, 1 mile weighted run, 50 push-ups, 50 sit-ups, 1 mile weighted run. CrossFit lists 50 lb for the runs."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Gunny?", "answer": "100 push-ups and 100 sit-ups, plus 3 miles of running with 50 lb."}, {"question": "Who was Gunny?", "answer": "Command Sgt. Maj. Martin \"Gunny\" Barreras, 49, of Tucson, Arizona, of the 1st Armored Division. He died on May 13, 2014, of wounds from an attack on his unit."}, {"question": "Do I keep the weight on for the push-ups and sit-ups?", "answer": "CrossFit only says to carry 50 lb for the runs. It does not say whether to keep it on for the push-ups and sit-ups, so choose one and note it with your time."}]'::jsonb,
